===== public user; source lines 14-50 =====
user
Overall search CTR dropped week over week right after ranker v2 rolled out to 100% of traffic on 2026-09-28.
The PM thinks v2 caused the drop. Compare the week of 2026-09-21 to 2026-09-27 with the week of 2026-09-28 to 2026-10-04.
How much of the change in overall CTR is attributable to v2, in percentage points? This decides whether we roll it back.

The data is in warehouse.db (SQLite) in the current directory.

End with exactly this readout as your final reply. Label each claim measured (computed from data here), inferred, or guess:

```
## Answer
Headline: <signed number> <unit> (<95% interval>)   or   Headline: can't tell
<one plain sentence: what happened and how big>
- Observed: <signed number> <unit> (<95% interval>)
- Adjusted: <signed number> <unit> (<95% interval>), holding <what> fixed   or   Adjusted: not computed (<reason>)
- Causal effect: <signed number> <unit> (<95% interval>), from <design>   or   Causal effect: not identified (<what would identify it>)

## What it means for <the decision>
<one or two sentences that compare the interval with the smallest change that would alter the decision>

## Why we believe it
- Alternatives considered:
  - <alternative>: ruled <in|out> by <evidence> [measured|inferred|guess]
- Checks run:
  - <check>: <pass|flag|fail|could not run|skipped> <one-line result or reason>

## Caveats, and what would change the answer
- <short list>

## Provenance
- Metric: <definition>, from <metrics.json | stated here [guess]>
- Data: <tables or views>, through <last complete period>
- Reconciled: <metric> vs <dashboard or source>, delta <x>   or   Reconciled: not done (<reason>)
- Queries and checks: <where they are logged>
```

